Coincident face winding, unlimited inputs, labeled arrangement export
(OpenMeshCraft @0e8d12c3, on top of 0001).

- Coincident triangles of different inputs are stored once; the winding of the second
  copy was dropped (pockets are keyed by their vertex set), so faces where two solids
  touch were treated like shared boundary: union kept an internal face, intersection
  returned a zero-volume sheet, subtraction left a hole. Record per triangle the inputs
  whose copy winds opposite (ArrLabels::opposite) and use it in the selection.
- Label becomes a dynamic bitset (no 32-input limit; up to 64 inputs stay inline).
- MeshBoolean::exportLabeledArrangement: after computeLabels(), export all arrangement
  triangles with their surface / inside / opposite labels so callers can apply their
  own selection.

